commit 7e94cf0eb7ec19bb4e5dea0a0d71e11544e2c003
Author: anyang-keepers <anyang.keepers@gmail.com>
Commit: GitHub <noreply@github.com>

    feat(schedule): add masc_schedule_note_add / masc_schedule_notes_list tools (task-381) (#35237)
    
    * feat(schedule): record schedule notes as append-only history in the store
    
    Notes are keyed by the stable schedule_id, not the per-instance id, so a
    definition replacement (masc_schedule_update) cannot orphan the prose that
    explains it. Appends bump the ledger version like any other mutation but
    bypass prune_completed, because a note's value is surviving terminal state.
    Ledgers written before this change decode with an empty note list.
    
    * feat(schedule): add masc_schedule_note_add and masc_schedule_notes_list tools
    
    Append-only notes keyed by schedule_id, surviving terminal states so
    replacements keep their history and woken keepers read why a schedule
    exists and what changed.
    
    - tool_schemas_schedule: two new schemas + published order growth
    - tool_schemas_schedule_toml: TOML parity with the rendered schemas
    - config/tools: masc_schedule_note_add.toml, masc_schedule_notes_list.toml
    - tool_catalog: note_add is a broadcast tool, notes_list a read
    - tool_catalog_surfaces: both registered on the schedule request surface
    - schedule_store: accept/fail/recover wake mutations persist their
      updated wakes into the bumped state
    - test_keeper_tool_schema_bytes: ceiling 103,716 -> 105,415 bytes across
      121 tools (+1,931 for the two tools)
    - dune-project: declare the vendored ocaml-msx package so sandboxes
      without the pinned switch can build; /vendor/ is gitignored and never
      committed, CI keeps using the pinned package
    
    * fix(schedule): annotate notes_list limit default as DET-OK
    
    The notes_list handler's pagination default (Option.value ~default:50)
    mirrors handle_list's bounded projection default and trips the
    determinism-contract ratchet. Document the rationale with a DET-OK
    comment so the gate passes without changing behavior.
    
